+### Hooks and post-rendering
+By default, post-renderers receive all rendered manifests, including those
+annotated as hooks, before Helm separates, sorts, and formats the final hook and
+non-hook outputs. This means a post-renderer can inspect and modify hook
+manifests just like any other manifest.
+
+To keep track of where each document came from, Helm annotates every rendered
+document with a `postrenderer.helm.sh/postrender-filename` annotation before
+passing it to the post-renderer, and removes that annotation again from the
+post-rendered output. Partial files (those whose base name starts with `_`) and
+empty rendered files are not sent to the post-renderer. If the post-renderer
+returns documents without the filename annotation, Helm includes them using
+generated filenames. Invalid YAML in the rendered templates or in the
+post-renderer output, as well as a non-zero exit from the post-renderer, cause
+the operation to fail with an error.
+
